1
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:04,159
Son, I'm back.

2
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,760
Are you home?

3
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,640
Dad's back.

4
00:01:22,599 --> 00:01:23,560
I'm exhausted.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,799
Son.

6
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,319
Fix me something to eat.

7
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:31,480
Go wash your hands.

8
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,000
You... this is all you eat when you're home alone?

9
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:36,799
Can't you make something better?

10
00:01:36,799 --> 00:01:37,879
Didn't Dad give you money?

11
00:01:37,879 --> 00:01:38,719
Go wash your hands.

12
00:01:39,319 --> 00:01:40,280
You're so fussy.

13
00:01:42,079 --> 00:01:43,799
Son, bring me the soap.

14
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,680
How many times have I told you?

15
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,959
It's called scented soap.

16
00:01:50,359 --> 00:01:51,400
What's wrong, son?

17
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:54,000
Turn around.

18
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,879
Is it because Dad's been away for so long?

19
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:11,599
Your favorite chocolate.

20
00:02:12,759 --> 00:02:13,319
Here.

21
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,560
Haven't you always wanted

22
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:21,439
a copy of "Three Hundred Tang Poems"?

23
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,919
It's an old book,

24
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,919
but the ancient poems inside are old too.

25
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:29,520
They read the same and can still be passed down.

26
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:34,919
Come on, son.

27
00:02:37,159 --> 00:02:37,719
Dad,

28
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,360
is it New Year's today?

29
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,719
This is better than New Year's.

30
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,000
What a huge trophy.

31
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,080
Son, you're amazing!

32
00:02:48,719 --> 00:02:51,280
My teacher said in less than two years,

33
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:53,639
I'll be a rising star in the literary world.

34
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:54,280
Really?

35
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,599
Son, you really are amazing.

36
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,960
You'll always be my pride and joy.

37
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,400
You'll always do me proud.

38
00:03:04,039 --> 00:03:05,520
This is great. Just great.

39
00:03:06,439 --> 00:03:08,120
I'll put it in the most prominent spot.

40
00:03:08,199 --> 00:03:08,719
Come on.

41
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,080
Make sure you get both of us.

42
00:03:10,919 --> 00:03:12,879
Alright, son, eat some more.

43
00:03:12,919 --> 00:03:13,879
Son, have some meat.

44
00:03:14,919 --> 00:03:15,439
Here.

45
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,120
Have some fish, son.

46
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:21,680
Here.

47
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,240
Bie Fan,

48
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:57,319
it's fine if it's empty,

49
00:04:59,959 --> 00:05:01,279
just pour me some more.

50
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:33,160
Dad.

51
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,800
Son.

52
00:05:35,519 --> 00:05:36,120
Dad.

53
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:36,800
Son.

54
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:37,879
Dad, I'm sorry.

55
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,959
I've made you wait here for me for so long.

56
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,639
You came here at such a young age.

57
00:05:46,639 --> 00:05:47,800
You didn't even live as long as I have.

58
00:05:48,959 --> 00:05:49,639
Dad.

59
00:05:51,879 --> 00:05:52,680
You have no idea.

60
00:05:54,959 --> 00:05:56,360
I'm so tired of living.

61
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:00,839
I haven't had a single happy day.

62
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,079
I play the writer for them,

63
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:06,839
and they play mind games with me.

64
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,560
Son.

65
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,000
Alright, alright.

66
00:06:26,879 --> 00:06:28,360
Let's stop talking about unpleasant things.

67
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,399
Come on, let's go inside.

68
00:06:37,759 --> 00:06:38,600
Xiao Ai.

69
00:06:38,879 --> 00:06:39,480
I'm here.

70
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:40,800
Play a tune.

71
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:41,920
Okay.

72
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,920
Playing "Going Home".

73
00:06:52,879 --> 00:06:54,240
This is Russian chocolate.

74
00:06:54,399 --> 00:06:55,600
This is German chocolate.

75
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,399
This is Swiss.

76
00:06:56,519 --> 00:06:57,199
Dutch.

77
00:06:57,319 --> 00:06:58,040
From Yiwu.

78
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,079
From the supermarket downstairs.

79
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:00,040
Anyway, everything you love to eat,

80
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,279
I bought it all for you.

81
00:07:14,839 --> 00:07:15,560
What's wrong?

82
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:16,519
It's expired.

83
00:07:16,959 --> 00:07:17,560
Delicious.

84
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,720
You call this delicious?

85
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:21,399
Son, look at this.

86
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,279
Let's go.

87
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,759
What now? You...

88
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:47,879
Dad, you've been here all along.

89
00:07:48,439 --> 00:07:50,199
I just wanted more time with you.

90
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:56,439
Dad.

91
00:07:57,399 --> 00:07:58,839
Didn't I throw these out ages ago?

92
00:07:59,519 --> 00:08:00,959
I picked them all back up for you.

93
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,680
If you don't want them, I do.

94
00:08:02,879 --> 00:08:04,040
They're all my pride and joy.

95
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,360
Your clippings from the newspaper,

96
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,480
I saved every one of them.

97
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:08,680
Maybe...

98
00:08:09,199 --> 00:08:10,399
in other people's eyes,

99
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:11,680
this is all trash.

100
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:13,800
But to me,

101
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:14,920
they're...

102
00:08:15,439 --> 00:08:17,839
treasures buried in the deep-sea mud.

103
00:08:18,519 --> 00:08:19,399
The Heart of the Ocean.

104
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,399
Come on, eat.

105
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:26,839
I saw it all.

106
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:28,560
When you're at work,

107
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,000
you barely eat or drink.

108
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,560
Starting today,

109
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,080
eat whatever you want.

110
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,360
Drink whatever you want.

111
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,159
Our good days are here.

112
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:41,759
Dad.

113
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,000
If I'd known you were over here

114
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,039
living like this,

115
00:08:46,279 --> 00:08:47,679
I'd have burned more for you.

116
00:08:48,639 --> 00:08:49,279
It's all good.

117
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,399
It's all good, Dad.

118
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,000
Good.

119
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,240
Such a big place, all to yourself?

120
00:08:55,639 --> 00:08:56,480
All these years,

121
00:08:57,679 --> 00:08:58,440
were you lonely?

122
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,840
I was extremely...

123
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,360
not lonely.

124
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,360
Let me introduce you to the neighbors.

125
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,240
We've got a newcomer!

126
00:09:07,559 --> 00:09:08,519
My son.

127
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,320
Haowen, let me introduce you.

128
00:09:11,639 --> 00:09:12,840
The one in green is Auntie Wang.

129
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,039
So you're Haowen.

130
00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:15,879
What a handsome young man.

131
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,039
I'll set you up with a girl sometime.

132
00:09:18,759 --> 00:09:20,200
The one with the round face is Auntie Li.

133
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:21,440
Haowen is here.

134
00:09:21,679 --> 00:09:23,000
Your dad talks about you all the time.

135
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,879
What a good-looking boy.

136
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,600
The one in the middle with the rectangular face

137
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,399
is Auntie Zhang.

138
00:09:28,039 --> 00:09:29,840
I've seen you in photos before.

139
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,840
Now I finally meet you in person.

140
00:09:32,279 --> 00:09:33,360
This is Auntie Shu.

141
00:09:38,519 --> 00:09:40,519
Dad, you seem different from

142
00:09:41,759 --> 00:09:42,480
what I imagined.

143
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,639
I have changed.

144
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:47,639
But my heart that loves you

145
00:09:48,399 --> 00:09:49,799
will never change.

146
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,039
Son.

147
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,679
The 20 billion you sent me,

148
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,320
I haven't spent a cent.

149
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,279
I've saved it all for you.

150
00:10:06,879 --> 00:10:08,279
I should've burned more for you.

151
00:10:08,279 --> 00:10:08,799
No.

152
00:10:09,559 --> 00:10:10,320
No.

153
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,799
No, no, no.

154
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:16,159
No, no, no.

155
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:21,919
No, no, no.

156
00:10:21,919 --> 00:10:22,679
No!

157
00:10:22,879 --> 00:10:23,919
Fang!

158
00:10:24,399 --> 00:10:25,600
Fang!

159
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,200
No, Fang!

160
00:10:27,399 --> 00:10:28,279
Fang!

161
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,399
F-Fang!

162
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:37,960
F-Fang, wake up!

163
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,120
Fang!

164
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,440
Stop hitting me! Stop!

165
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:44,480
Am I dead?

166
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,080
How am I still alive?

167
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:52,480
You jumped off that bridge just now

168
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:54,840
and went headfirst into the mud.

169
00:10:57,519 --> 00:10:59,039
Then I had no other choice.

170
00:11:03,279 --> 00:11:05,320
I went to a nearby house

171
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,320
and found a rope.

172
00:11:06,759 --> 00:11:08,519
I climbed down and lassoed you,

173
00:11:08,519 --> 00:11:09,879
then dragged you to the bank.

174
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,360
And then I dragged you ashore.

175
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,600
And then I... I saw you weren't breathing.

176
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,399
I just... just...

177
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,240
scooped the mud in your mouth...

178
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,679
and just... dug it out.

179
00:11:29,919 --> 00:11:31,039
I'm so glad you're not dead.

180
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,279
I'll take you to get washed up.

181
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:32,879
Let's go.

182
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,519
And some Aunt Liu...

183
00:11:35,519 --> 00:11:36,200
Aunt Liu.

184
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:37,200
Aunt Li.

185
00:11:38,279 --> 00:11:39,240
Right, Aunt Li.

186
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:40,799
And Aunt Wang.

187
00:11:41,039 --> 00:11:43,279
Let's go somewhere else, they're closed.

188
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,039
And a room full of money.

189
00:11:46,559 --> 00:11:47,720
A big room full of money.

190
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,559
He jumped off the bridge.

191
00:11:49,559 --> 00:11:51,279
And now we probably need to...

192
00:11:51,879 --> 00:11:52,679
wash up a bit.

193
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,679
Remember to give it back later.

194
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,720
Okay, thanks.

195
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:03,960
Fang.

196
00:12:04,919 --> 00:12:05,919
Change your glasses.

197
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,360
Want a polish?

198
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,159
No. You really think you're washing a car?

199
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,000
How about some wax then?

200
00:13:25,879 --> 00:13:26,720
Here, have a smoke.

201
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,039
Dad

202
00:13:41,919 --> 00:13:42,720
I'm here

203
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,200
I...

204
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,159
Fang.

205
00:14:01,399 --> 00:14:02,080
I'm looking for...

206
00:14:02,399 --> 00:14:06,320
I want... I'm looking for my dad.

207
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:07,559
Hand it over.

208
00:14:07,799 --> 00:14:08,519
Grab him!

209
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,919
I'm just trying to save...

210
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:10,720
You guys...

211
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:13,919
Let... let go!

212
00:14:13,919 --> 00:14:14,600
Fang!

213
00:14:22,399 --> 00:14:23,240
My dad's car.

214
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,080
Boss, wash the car!

215
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:28,320
Anyone washing cars here?

216
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,519
Didn't you hear me? Wash the car!

217
00:14:29,519 --> 00:14:30,120
Dad!

218
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,360
My dad's here to pick me up!

219
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,360
Who is this?

220
00:14:35,559 --> 00:14:37,639
He's sick. Bipolar.

221
00:14:38,679 --> 00:14:39,279
He has a mental illness.

222
00:14:39,279 --> 00:14:40,480
I don't care what he has!

223
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,919
Keep him away from my car.

224
00:14:42,039 --> 00:14:43,919
If it gets scratched... this is Bin's car!

225
00:14:43,919 --> 00:14:45,279
This is my... my dad's car.

226
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,399
This is my dad's car.

227
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,840
My dad's car.

228
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,279
I'm telling you, it's my dad's car!

229
00:14:51,279 --> 00:14:53,639
My dad's! My dad's!

230
00:14:54,679 --> 00:14:55,320
This is my...

231
00:15:01,799 --> 00:15:02,639
It's not my dad's car.

232
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,480
The little gold man is different.

233
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:09,720
Don't touch it!

234
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:11,519
If you dare touch this car today,

235
00:15:12,159 --> 00:15:13,399
I'll kill you.

236
00:15:20,799 --> 00:15:21,519
Do it.

237
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,519
Hit me!

238
00:16:02,639 --> 00:16:03,559
Hello, Boss. Big brother.

239
00:16:04,799 --> 00:16:05,879
Fang.

240
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,679
Kick his leg off!

241
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,879
What? Why'd you break off my golden man?

242
00:16:46,759 --> 00:16:47,960
Take that cloth off.

243
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,840
That blondie of yours said

244
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,240
breaking off that car emblem of yours

245
00:16:58,519 --> 00:16:59,279
would get me killed.

246
00:17:00,279 --> 00:17:01,000
Real tough guys, huh?

247
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,399
Come on, do it. Don't hold back.

248
00:17:02,639 --> 00:17:03,480
Come on, kill me! Come on!

249
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,480
How is he so cocky on our turf?

250
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,279
You have no idea that right now I...

251
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:10,720
This guy is out of his mind.

252
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:12,480
No.

253
00:17:12,559 --> 00:17:15,400
My... my brain is broken.

254
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,279
He has a condition.

255
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,640
Bipolar disorder.

256
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:22,440
Let me show you guys something.

257
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:27,920
The farce of washed-up author Fang Haowen

258
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:28,839
continues to escalate.

259
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,039
Some experts claim he is

260
00:17:30,039 --> 00:17:31,440
suffering from a mental disorder.

261
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:32,799
He slapped judge Hei Cong

262
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,079
and author Ren Fangfang.

263
00:17:34,079 --> 00:17:35,880
He even caused a scene at a school cafeteria,

264
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,119
wielding filthy objects

265
00:17:37,119 --> 00:17:38,400
polluting the future of our nation.

266
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,680
Got it. Turn it off.

267
00:17:44,079 --> 00:17:46,359
I get it. His situation...

268
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,440
Is pretty serious.

269
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,920
Since the law is involved...

270
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,279
there's nothing I can do.

271
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,759
My golden statue...

272
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,440
Is just a total loss.

273
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:57,640
Why is he jumping around like that?

274
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,279
Does he have some kind of demand or what?

275
00:17:59,279 --> 00:18:00,000
Kill me!

276
00:18:01,279 --> 00:18:02,839
He wants to kill himself.

277
00:18:03,079 --> 00:18:04,839
He doesn't want to live anymore.

278
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,640
So...

279
00:18:07,799 --> 00:18:09,799
This is his suicide note.

280
00:18:12,599 --> 00:18:13,559
Where did you get that note?

281
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:15,559
Give that note back to me!

282
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:16,680
Bring the note to me, you hear?

283
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,519
I'm here.

284
00:18:17,519 --> 00:18:18,279
Give it to me.

285
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,480
Read it.

286
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,440
Okay.

287
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:29,240
A final note to the world. Fang Haowen.

288
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:32,079
Alias: The Lone Hermit.

289
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,240
This letter...

290
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:38,599
Is the last voice I leave to this world.

291
00:18:38,759 --> 00:18:41,519
By the time you read these words,

292
00:18:41,599 --> 00:18:44,000
I will have shed this mortal coil.

293
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,920
I, Fang Haowen,

294
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,920
have read extensively since childhood.

295
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:51,240
While others shy away from those erotic ancient texts...

296
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,640
Esoteric! Esoteric! Esoteric!

297
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:57,160
I can immerse myself in them,

298
00:18:57,359 --> 00:18:59,039
converse with ancient sages,

299
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,079
and absorb the nutrients of wisdom.

300
00:19:01,279 --> 00:19:02,839
These classic literary works,

301
00:19:02,839 --> 00:19:04,000
to me,

302
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,480
are not just cold words stuck together...

303
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,599
I mean... stacked!

304
00:19:08,799 --> 00:19:12,440
Right. But rather a deep exchange with great souls.

305
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,079
I once thought

306
00:19:14,279 --> 00:19:16,759
with my talent and hard work,

307
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:19,160
making a mark in the literary world

308
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,599
was only a matter

309
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:22,920
of time.

310
00:19:23,599 --> 00:19:26,839
So, I wrote day and night without pause,

311
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:30,279
pouring all my thoughts,

312
00:19:30,279 --> 00:19:31,799
feelings, and realizations

313
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:34,720
unreservedly into my pen.

314
00:19:35,839 --> 00:19:36,480
However,

315
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:42,480
reality was like a heavy slap

316
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:45,640
viciously striking my face.

317
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,079
I hit walls everywhere,

318
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,319
no one appreciated me,

319
00:19:50,599 --> 00:19:51,759
no one understood me.

320
00:19:52,319 --> 00:19:53,440
The pressures of life

321
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,599
surged toward me like a tide,

322
00:19:57,319 --> 00:19:58,759
suffocating me.

323
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:00,880
To make a living,

324
00:20:01,839 --> 00:20:03,000
I had to livestream.

325
00:20:03,079 --> 00:20:04,160
I had to sell products.

326
00:20:04,319 --> 00:20:07,720
I had to pander to those pompous fools.

327
00:20:10,039 --> 00:20:10,880
I can't accept this!

328
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:12,319
I just can't accept it!

329
00:20:12,319 --> 00:20:13,759
Am I not more talented

330
00:20:13,759 --> 00:20:15,440
than those so-called famous writers

331
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,319
and literary giants?

332
00:20:17,319 --> 00:20:19,200
Are my works

333
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:22,359
not deeper than theirs?

334
00:20:22,359 --> 00:20:23,720
not more profound?

335
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:25,000
But they

336
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,359
exploit me,

337
00:20:30,599 --> 00:20:31,480
insult me,

338
00:20:33,079 --> 00:20:35,319
mock me, and then reap fame and fortune!

339
00:20:35,319 --> 00:20:38,079
While I can only hide in a cold corner

340
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:41,319
and cry alone.

341
00:20:44,279 --> 00:20:45,880
This world is too unfair.

342
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:48,039
It has no room for true art.

343
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:49,599
It has no room for someone like me

344
00:20:49,599 --> 00:20:51,039
who stays true to his original passion.

345
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:52,519
My original dreams

346
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,839
under the grind of time,

347
00:20:56,359 --> 00:20:57,759
have been shattered to pieces.

348
00:20:58,079 --> 00:21:00,599
Now, I am physically and mentally exhausted,

349
00:21:00,599 --> 00:21:02,599
and completely despair of this world.

350
00:21:03,319 --> 00:21:03,960
I'm leaving.

351
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:07,960
With pride,

352
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,400
with resentment,

353
00:21:10,359 --> 00:21:11,000
with...

354
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:11,519
just lingering.

355
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,759
But I firmly believe

356
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:15,599
that my soul

357
00:21:16,079 --> 00:21:18,960
will live forever in the world of words.

358
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,279
Oh, right.

359
00:21:21,799 --> 00:21:22,759
After I die,

360
00:21:23,079 --> 00:21:25,680
I've left the copyright of my second book

361
00:21:27,079 --> 00:21:28,720
to the most important person in my life.

362
00:21:29,119 --> 00:21:31,119
If by some fluke, people still like it,

363
00:21:31,119 --> 00:21:33,680
I hope she can set up a

364
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:36,400
Fang Haowen Cultural Scholarship Fund,

365
00:21:36,519 --> 00:21:38,480
to be a beacon for kids who love literature

366
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,920
but have no way out.

367
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:42,599
If,

368
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,119
one day, those kids want to find me,

369
00:21:46,079 --> 00:21:47,559
please go to my hometown,

370
00:21:48,839 --> 00:21:51,160
Fangjiatun, Xing County, Hachun City.

371
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,839
On the fifth mountain left of Yaolong Ridge,

372
00:21:54,519 --> 00:21:56,119
by the tree on the mountainside,

373
00:21:58,119 --> 00:21:59,559
plant a bamboo stick.

374
00:22:03,519 --> 00:22:04,400
May you all

375
00:22:07,119 --> 00:22:10,759
stand firm through countless trials,

376
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:18,839
no matter which way the wind blows.

377
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,240
You've been rambling for ages.

378
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,240
Did I tell you to speak?

379
00:22:33,119 --> 00:22:33,799
Right.

380
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:36,240
This is his suicide note.

381
00:22:36,359 --> 00:22:37,400
Word for word.

382
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,640
He really wants to die.

383
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,839
He doesn't want to die.

384
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:43,000
He's been mumbling and reading this forever.

385
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,920
If this were a TV show, half an episode would be gone by now.

386
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,559
If he really wanted to die, why write a note?

387
00:22:46,759 --> 00:22:48,880
Just grab a knife and slit your throat, much faster!

388
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,200
I really do want to die!

389
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,920
Why exactly do you want to die?

390
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,880
Bro, I've been reading this note for half an episode.

391
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,119
Did you not listen to a single word?

392
00:23:06,119 --> 00:23:08,720
I heard it loud and clear. You...

393
00:23:09,359 --> 00:23:10,480
You're not a bad guy.

394
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,240
And you're not crazy either.

395
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,880
You're just being petty.

396
00:23:15,799 --> 00:23:17,079
Wrote a little essay,

397
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:19,160
think it shows off your literary talent, right?

398
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,880
People don't understand you, don't appreciate you.

399
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,119
So you get all petty.

400
00:23:23,119 --> 00:23:24,480
And just want to die, right?

401
00:23:25,319 --> 00:23:28,200
Listen, bro. Haowen, right?

402
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:30,799
No matter what happens in life,

403
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
you can't just throw your life away.

404
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,480
Look at yourself.

405
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,039
You're still perfectly intact, aren't you?

406
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:37,920
Now look at me.

407
00:23:38,119 --> 00:23:39,440
Look at my hand.

408
00:23:39,559 --> 00:23:42,000
Y-y-you know how I got this?

409
00:23:42,799 --> 00:23:43,680
Ever since I was a kid...

410
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,680
I didn't want anyone bullying me.

411
00:23:46,119 --> 00:23:47,359
So I picked fights with people.

412
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:50,799
H-h-how many bricks have I taken to the head?

413
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:53,359
And those bricks always hit the right side of my brain.

414
00:23:53,559 --> 00:23:55,240
Ended up giving me Parkinson's!

415
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:57,960
Even so, I still love life!

416
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,720
I still gotta give back to society!

417
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,720
And look at my grandpa's time.

418
00:24:03,319 --> 00:24:05,319
They had no food, no water.

419
00:24:06,039 --> 00:24:07,599
Eating a piece of cornbread every day

420
00:24:07,799 --> 00:24:08,920
was like celebrating New Year's.

421
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:10,720
Now look at you!

422
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,160
Eating so well every day, all plump and pale.

423
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,079
And you still want to die?

424
00:24:13,079 --> 00:24:14,359
Then look at my...

425
00:24:14,359 --> 00:24:16,119
grandpa's grandpa's grandpa.

426
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:18,160
They didn't even have shoes back then.

427
00:24:18,319 --> 00:24:20,000
They wore nothing but straw ropes.

428
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,480
Look at you, wearing a tuxedo!

429
00:24:22,759 --> 00:24:24,240
with two curtains hanging off your ass!

430
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,559
Th-th-that grandpa's grandpa...

431
00:24:25,559 --> 00:24:26,000
Th-th-they...

432
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,359
were lucky just to have a flap to cover their ass!

433
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:29,640
Why don't you cherish

434
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,359
the happy life you have right now?

435
00:24:31,559 --> 00:24:33,240
Why ruin a perfectly good life?

436
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,359
Your grandpas had it rough.

437
00:24:34,359 --> 00:24:35,240
Exactly.

438
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,839
Grandpas, our first time meeting, I'll take a bow.

439
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,119
This kid isn't bad at heart.

440
00:24:41,119 --> 00:24:43,920
Bro, I'll say hi to your grandpas for you.

441
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:45,480
Alright then, thanks.

442
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,799
Grandpas!

443
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:50,319
Here I come!

444
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,400
What the hell is he doing?

445
00:25:11,359 --> 00:25:13,319
The grandpas are gone.

446
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:16,039
They're all burned up! Grandpas...

447
00:25:16,039 --> 00:25:18,799
My grandpas! Grandpas! Grandpas!

448
00:25:23,319 --> 00:25:25,200
Mothers suffer the most giving birth.

449
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:26,880
He doesn't value life,

450
00:25:27,319 --> 00:25:28,480
and he doesn't respect his mom.

451
00:25:28,799 --> 00:25:30,079
He should experience

452
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,799
the pain of a mother giving birth.

453
00:25:32,319 --> 00:25:33,279
I looked it up.

454
00:25:33,279 --> 00:25:34,039
The AI said

455
00:25:34,039 --> 00:25:35,599
electric shocks can usually match

456
00:25:35,599 --> 00:25:36,559
the pain of giving birth.

457
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:38,880
Bie Fan.

458
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,359
What are you doing, Bie Fan?

459
00:25:43,519 --> 00:25:44,680
Do you still want to die?

460
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:47,000
Do you want to die?
